As a benchmark reaction, 4-methoxystyrene was used as a substrate with $\mathrm{CF}_{3}\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{I}$ in acetonitrile $\mathrm{\langleH_{2}O}$ under visible-light irradiation, with N, Ndiisopropylethylamine as a base.  These reactions were monitored by use of gas chromatography-mass spectrometry (GC-MS).  Using UiO- $67\mathrm{-Ir(ppy)}_{2}$ $20\%$ loading after PSM, ${\sim}5\ \mathrm{mol}\%$ Ir), quantitative conversion resulted in a $60\%$ yield of the hydroxytrifluoroethyl product A (Table 1, Entry 4).  Encouragingly, UiO-67- $\mathrm{\dot{Ir}(p p y^{F})}_{2}$ $9\%$ loading after PSM, ${\sim}5~\mathrm{mol}\%$ Ir) was able to improve the yield of the desired product $\mathbf{A}$ to $76\%$ (Table 1, Entry 5).  By comparison, three homogeneous photocatalysts: $\mathrm{{Ir}(p p y)_{3}}$ , $\mathrm{[Ir(ppy)_{2}(E t_{2}d c b p y)]C l,}$ $\mathrm{\dot{[}I r(p p y^{F})_{2}(E t_{2}d c b p y)]C i}$ (Scheme 1) were employed to catalyze the same reaction, but these produced a high yield of an undesired dimerization side product C, with only $10\%$ , $20\%$ , and $32\%$ yields of the preferred hy
